 ck-transform)\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } Abou
 t the Book In Confessions of a Recovering Engineer: Transportation for a S
 trong Town\, author and urbanist Charles L. Marohn\, Jr. delivers an acces
 sible and engaging exploration of America's transportation system. He lays
  bare the reasons why transit no longer works as it once did\, and envisio
 ns how to modernize transportation to better serve local communities. In t
 he book\, you’ll discover real-world examples of poor transportation des
 ign choices that have had dramatic and tragic effects. You'll also find ex
 amples of design improvements that have revitalized communities and improv
 ed safety. #block-f1e6baa8db82f92cb47e { --stroke-style: none\;--stroke-th
